{"term":"seep","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:6e1a84fd81748a68b4","definition":"To ooze or pass slowly through pores or other small openings, and in overly small quantities; said of liquids, etc.","example":"Water has seeped through the roof.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["leak"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":["seeper","seepweed","seepy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seep#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b525756af3fca998ee","definition":"To enter or penetrate slowly; to spread or diffuse.","example":"Woe seeped through her heart thinking of what had befallen their ethnic group.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["leak"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":["seeper","seepweed","seepy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seep#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7e36c67ef4dcf5fc03","definition":"To diminish or wane away slowly.","example":"The resistance movement against the invaders had slowly seeped away.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["leak"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"figuratively","register":"figuratively, intransitive","wordFamily":["seeper","seepweed","seepy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/seep#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:be237fc3d8ba6aa0ca","definition":"(of a crack etc.) To allow a liquid to pass through, to leak.","example":"The crack is seeping water.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["leak"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":["seeper","seepweed","seepy"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","so